    <item>
      <title>Internship Reflection</title>
      <link>https://ryankembrey.github.io/internship-reflection/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://ryankembrey.github.io/internship-reflection/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;what-were-your-expectations-about-your-internship-before-you-joined&#34;&gt;What were your expectations about your internship before you joined?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The internship was not initially meant to be one. I applied for a role as a production engineer at
Xero Linear Lighting Systems, and during the interview, told them I was looking to complete an
internship. We agreed to consider this role an internship, although the work duties did not
majorly change based off the original job description.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;what-was-the-reality-how-was-it-different-from-your-expectations&#34;&gt;What was the reality? How was it different from your expectations?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The place I worked at made architectural lighting installations. There was a team of 4 engineers
who worked upstairs (along with other managing people), and downstairs was a factory for
producing these installations. For the first 3 months, I worked as production assistant in the
factory completing repetitive manual labour duties. This included filing, deburring, assembling,
sanding, bending sheet metal, and a small amount of time shadowing the CNC operator. The
intention behind this first placement was to gain valuable hands-on experience, in order to better
perform the duties of an engineer upstairs. My expectation was to move on quickly to perform the
duties advertised, such as drafting, CAD work, engineering documentation, and process
improvement; but unfortunately, management got comfortable having me work downstairs, despite
me advocating for myself. After much deliberation, I was finally moved upstairs, where I worked
for 2 months, until I was asked to take a week off due to low sales, then ghosted by my manager.
Luckily I had already completed my required hours for the internship, and was just continuing
work there beyond the internship at this stage. It was an unfortunate end to my first placement in
industry.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
